# Security boundary

- Never create, request, display, store or commit secrets, `.env` values,
  tokens, cookies, passwords, seed/private keys, wallet recovery or signer data.
- Operate inside one elected repository/worktree. Never track absolute machine
  paths, usernames or account identifiers.
- Provider/API/RPC/WSS, credentials, packages, purchases, deployment,
  settings, wallet/signer/transaction and real money require the exact gate.
- Routine bounded GitHub delivery transport is allowed; unrelated discovery or
  account/repository mutation is not.
- Exception text and raw sensitive values never enter receipts.
